een_point_and_line_011","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Why is the closest displacement vector from a point to a line orthogonal to the line direction?","options":["Orthogonality is irrelevant for shortest distance.","The closest displacement must equal the direction vector.","The closest displacement must be parallel to the line direction.","Any component along the line can be removed to make the segment shorter."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"12968f7b31fec526d9cd0238","time_limit":30},{"id":"la_batch14_distance_between_point_and_line_015","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"What is the distance from $(1,0)$ to the line $y=x$?","options":["$\\sqrt{2}$","$\\frac{1}{2}$","$1$","$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"977bdfee71303702fa2274b4","time_limit":30},{"id":"la_batch14_distance_between_point_and_line_017","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Why does the point-line distance depend on the whole line and not on a particular parametrisation of it?","options":["Changing parametrisation changes the geometric line.","Different parametrisations can describe the same set of points.","The parameter value itself is the distance.","Only the starting point of a parametrisation matters."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"537c43d973a81dd43a9a0d26","time_limit":40},{"id":"la_batch14_distance_between_point_and_line_020_curated20261027_001","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"The line $\\boldsymbol{\\ell}(t)=\\boldsymbol{B}+t\\boldsymbol{v}$ has $\\boldsymbol{B}=(0,0)$ and $\\boldsymbol{v}=(1,2)$. What is the foot $\\boldsymbol{F}$ of the perpendicular from $\\boldsymbol{A}=(5,0)$ to the line?","options":["$(1,2)$","$(5,10)$","$(\\sqrt{5},2\\sqrt{5})$","$(0,0)$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"eaad9662e32d7689f328cbc0","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1b_math_ii_linear_algebra_distance_betwe